{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Whoever raised the offering of silver and bronze.</b> The silver, and all the more so the bronze — each of them was more abundant than the gold, for gold was found only among the women in their ornaments, whereas silver and bronze were plentiful among most people in utensils and in coin. Therefore regarding silver and bronze Scripture uses the term תרומה (offering), while regarding gold it uses the term תנופה (waving), denoting elevation and distinction — for whoever donates gold waves his hand to raise his gift aloft, and those who receive it publicize it, to proclaim the merit of the donor. And even though we find the term תנופה used for bronze, as it is written (Exodus 38:29): ״ונחשת התנופה שבעים ככר״, Scripture used the term תנופה there for the distinction of that particular bronze, for it was burnished and exceedingly radiant, and was thus very precious and valuable, for gold was more commonly available than it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:21.285181663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}